Section: 2.1 Protecting the individual
Text: Promotion of knowledge and application of best-of-class approaches to health data is seen as one of the ethical duties of researchers (Duquenoy et al., 2008; Lawrence, 2016). But for this to be put in practice, ways need to be guar- anteed (e.g. with government help) to provide re- searchers with access to the relevant data. Re- searchers can also go to the data rather than have the data sent to them.

